T*
(KNOWN RISKS AND RECOMMENDED NEXT WORK) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(1. Persistence health: a failed temp-file write or rename preserves the old valid state) Tj
T*
(file, so atomicity is retained, but the newest state may not be durable. Add persistence) Tj
T*
(health status, an admin-visible warning, exponential retry backoff, and stale) Tj
T*
(temporary-file cleanup.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(2. Hashing backpressure: asynchronous hashing avoids blocking the event loop but does) Tj
T*
(not make hashing free. Add a bounded global hash/registration queue with a small) Tj
T*
(concurrency limit and a 503/Retry-After response when saturated. Do not blindly increase) Tj
T*
(UV_THREADPOOL_SIZE without retesting CPU and memory on the event laptop.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(3. Realistic benchmark: add a k6 scenario where each participant registers only once and) Tj
T*
(then polls. Test 50 and 75 teams on the actual event laptop and venue router. The) Tj
T*
(existing 150-VU continuous registration script is a useful breaking-point test, not a) Tj
T*
(check-in simulation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(4. Large-event scaling: for several hundred active teams, move sessions/state to Redis) Tj
T*
(and durable data to a database, and replace frequent polling with WebSockets or) Tj
T*
(Server-Sent Events.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
